diagnostics/error-checking.em:1:7: only an Error can be raised, but this is Int
  raise 1
        ^
Raise an Error value, such as `Error("what went wrong")`.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:2:1: a bare `raise` needs an error being handled
  raise
  ^^^^^
Use `raise SomeError("message")`, or put the bare `raise` inside a `catch` block.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:2:1: warning: this code can never run
  raise
  ^^^^^
Every path above it already returns, raises, breaks, or continues. Remove it, or move it earlier.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:6:14: a catch type must be an Error, but this is Int
  catch error: Int {
               ^^^
Catch `Error`, or a class that extends it.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:11:1: this catch already handles every Error
  catch error {
  ^^^^^
Move the untyped catch after the typed catches.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:16:8: a condition must be a Bool, but this is Int
  assert 1, 2
         ^
Compare it to something, as in `count > 0`. Emerald has no truthy or falsey values.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:16:11: an assertion message must be a String, but this is Int
  assert 1, 2
            ^
Write the explanation in quotes.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:22:9: `return` cannot leave a `finally` block
          return
          ^^^^^^
Finish the cleanup block normally, then return after it.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:31:11: `assigned_inside` may not have been assigned
      print(assigned_inside)
            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Assign `assigned_inside` on every branch before reading it.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:42:1: a test function cannot take parameters
  @test
  ^^^^^
Remove the parameters; each test must be runnable on its own.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:46:1: a test function cannot return a value
  @test
  ^^^^^
Remove the returned value; use `assert` to check the result inside the test.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:60:7: `MissingConstructor` needs a constructor, because building `DetailedError` takes arguments
  class MissingConstructor extends DetailedError {
        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
Add a constructor to `MissingConstructor` that starts with `super(...)`, passing what `DetailedError` needs.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:68:13: `break` cannot leave a `finally` block
              break
              ^^^^^
Finish the cleanup block normally. A loop entirely inside `finally` may still use `break`.
diagnostics/error-checking.em:78:13: `continue` cannot leave a `finally` block
              continue
              ^^^^^^^^
Finish the cleanup block normally. A loop entirely inside `finally` may still use `continue`.
